RD05 v34 CPU-port, RGMII timing and persistent overlay correction

Network datapath
----------------
The stable topology remains RTL8197F physical P0/RGMII to RTL8367D CPU7/EXT1.
Linux DSA supplies and consumes the 8-byte rtl8_4 tag. Hardware TX insertion
and RX tag removal therefore remain disabled on the RTL8197F side.

v33 hardware confirmation:
- CPUICR1 accepted 0x002081d3 after DMA start (8-dword TX/RX descriptors);
- CPURPDCR0 and CPUTPDCR0 accepted the actual ring bases;
- the diagnostic window contained no new peer/LAN2 traffic, so it could not
  prove or disprove switch-to-SoC RX packet delivery.

The same trace recorded FCS errors on RTL8367D CPU7 while receiving frames from
the SoC. v34 moves the EXT1 receive sampling delay from tap 5 to adjacent tap 6.
This targets the measured SoC-to-switch timing error without changing DSA tags,
VLAN membership, descriptor format or the switch-to-SoC receive direction.

Expected markers after LAN is brought up:
  RD05 DSA master v34: ...
  rd05 p0 rgmii v34: ... cputag-rx=1 preserve-tag=1 ...
  rd05 poststart v34: ... cpuicr1=0x002081d3 rxbase=... txbase=...

Persistent overlay
------------------
Only the RD05 rootfs_data range is writable:
  offset 0x00e60000
  size   0x001a0000

The v33 log returned the identical raw status word 0x00000004 after every WREN.
That does not prove which status bit or command write width the controller uses.
v34 therefore calibrates non-destructively before the first erase/program:

  WRDI -> RDSR -> WREN -> RDSR -> WRDI -> RDSR -> WREN -> RDSR

It tests the Realtek GPL SDK command placement (32-bit high byte) first, then
8-, 16- and 32-bit-low alternatives. A clear/set/clear/set transition must be
observed in the same status bit; static protection bits cannot pass this test.
No erase or page program is issued until calibration succeeds.

Expected success marker:
  calibrated SPI-NOR WEL: cmd=... lane=... bit=... before=... after=...

Expected overlay result:
  /dev/mtd8 exists
  /overlay is mounted from rootfs_data/JFFS2
  no "unable to calibrate SPI-NOR WEL" or JFFS2 errno -5 messages

Run:
  rd05-v34-check
  rd05-netdiag full

Use the PC companion during the full traffic window. A router cannot generate
proof of inbound LAN traffic by itself.
